      "writtenOn": "2018-01-18T23:42:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "NOT_READY is the initial state always, and it does not make sense to broadcast in cases where say the SIM is ABSENT. And even when the SIM goes to IO_ERROR or RESTRICTED or PRESENT state, without a broadcast it is understood that the application state is NOT_READY until a better state (LOCKED/LOADED) is broadcast. However going out of one of these states, we will broadcast NOT_READY, for example we may do that on SIM_REFRESH scenarios.",
